WEBVTT

00:15:59.615 --> 00:16:01.821
can help you focus
on the kinds of similarities

00:16:01.845 --> 00:16:04.423
that are useful to assess
in structured interviews.

00:16:04.447 --> 00:16:06.858
But I'm wondering, is that enough?

00:16:07.459 --> 00:16:08.790
Even with better questions,

00:16:08.814 --> 00:16:11.059
can we humans really overcome our biases?

00:16:11.373 --> 00:16:13.666
Siri: I don't think you can, Adam.

00:16:13.690 --> 00:16:14.941
AG: Siri?

00:16:14.965 --> 00:16:16.123
Siri: Hi, Adam.

00:16:16.147 --> 00:16:18.646
I hacked your episode
because I might have a solution

00:16:18.670 --> 00:16:20.463
for your irrational judgments.

00:16:21.241 --> 00:16:23.287
Me. Ha ha ha.

00:16:23.311 --> 00:16:25.804
But more on that after the break.

00:16:25.828 --> 00:16:32.802
(Music)